===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*warþō}}, an extension of a stem-verb {{m|gem-pro|*warōną||be on guard}} (whence {{term|warian}}). Cognate with Old High German {{m|goh|warta||watch}} (German {{m|de|Warte||watchtower}}), Old Saxon {{m|osx|warda}} (Middle Dutch {{m|dum|warde}}), Old Norse {{m|non|varða||cairn}}.

